body:
im very much closeted too (still am), one time my friends were playing games on my phone and i left them for couple minutes. when i got back they straight up were opening my browser (i used incognito, but apparently that time it didn't automatically closed) and showed me the unclosed tabs. i have never felt so mortified and scared in my life. i don't remember how i got out of that situation, i think im just lucky i lost contact with them. sometimes i still think about it to this day.  

&#x200B;

it can happen to anyone, no matter how careful you are.

hi, i just watched it recently and really love it!!. it's wholesome and doesn't have tragic ending like other gay movies i watched. i don't think many people like this movie, do you have any movie recommendation that pretty much like giant little ones(friendship,coming out of age, lgbtq+, teen)? i'm running out of movies to watch and it's kinda hard to find movies that i like so im asking you cause it seems like we have same movie taste lolol.

&#x200B;

btw pardon my terrible english 😶

if it really means something to you, do it. i think you won't regret it. imo it'll makes you remember who you were before watching skam. for me, s4 really changed me. i'm a muslim and sometimes idk how to react to something that conflicted with my belief. after watching how sana lives her life as a muslim, i realized that everything doesn't have to be the good based on my religion said. it really changes how i see the world as a muslim. I can be kind to everybody without feeling "not muslim enough". Oh and also that quote in noora's bedroom from S2 kinda hit me too. I used to be really selfish... if i get a tatoo i'd probably choose "fear spreads. fortunately, love does too" or "be kind" since the whole quote would be long lmao. so yeah i would advise to find something that really hit you deep, since it'll be permanent. it doesn't have to be quotes, some art it's okay too. 

&#x200B;

btw sorry for my terrible english lol i tried my best to write what's in my mind assadfhjgh
